# .dev.vars.example - SANDBOX/TEST secrets template. Placeholders only, NO real values.
#
# Copy this to `.dev.vars` (the real file is gitignored and never committed), then replace each
# `__REPLACE_ME__` with YOUR value. Deploy uploads them: `npx wrangler deploy --secrets-file .dev.vars`.
# These names come from wrangler.jsonc BASE `secrets.required`. Secret VALUES live only in `.dev.vars`,
# never here and never in git.

# Fine-grained GitHub PAT - resource owner = your org, repository access = Public repositories (the minimal option),
# organization permissions = Members: Read and write. (Same key in both envs; the value may differ.)
GITHUB_TOKEN=__REPLACE_ME__

# Stripe webhook signing secret (whsec_…) from THIS env's Stripe webhook.
# In this sandbox/test file: the TEST-mode secret. (In .dev.vars.production.example: the LIVE secret.)
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=__REPLACE_ME__

# Webhook URL path segment for /wh/stripe/<this>. NOT a worker secret (HMAC sig is the gate); it only
# lives in your Stripe webhook URL. Generate: openssl rand -hex 16. Kept commented just so you don't
# lose it - the worker never reads it.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_PATH="REPLACE_WITH_openssl_rand_-hex_16"

# OPTIONAL - outbound signed event delivery. Only set this if you also set `eventWebhook.url` in
# src/config/repoaccess.config.ts (the destination is config, not an env var).
# It is intentionally NOT in `secrets.required` (opt-in); leave it commented out if you don't use it.
# EVENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=__REPLACE_ME__
